{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "All 12 required pairs are retained. Their NOT_APPLICABLE findings concern these two claims only; they do not establish overall candidate fidelity or justify deleting either claim.",
    "The marketing claim's missing-paragraph uncertainty is resolved by the supplied services context in u3.792 and marketing provisions in u20.5257–u22.6374. Neither those provisions nor the supplied footnotes make truthful advertising an exception to the gift restriction.",
    "Scope placement changes outcomes: node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e places offering in scope; node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5, node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5, node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f and node.bca408c75cbf8467afafada6 place promotional conditions in scope. Known absence returns OUT_OF_SCOPE instead of the stated negative prohibition or positive compliance answer. An intentional domain restriction and a mismatch with the typed question remain competing interpretations.",
    "Unknown scope also prevents otherwise decisive result evaluation. For example, an unknown offer occurrence in node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e returns UNKNOWN even for a known non-gift. These candidates are not interchangeable under their declared runtime semantics.",
    "Both offer-level candidates combine an offer-level promotional connection with an existential non-discount gift classification. In mixed offers, the gift satisfying that existential condition must itself have the required promotional connection. Otherwise, an unrelated gift could trigger an unsupported prohibition. The representations do not expressly settle this connection.",
    "In node.142f34016b300f5c110eb249, 'provider' must identify the distributor making the offer. Requiring that distributor also to fund or fulfil the benefit would add an unsupported prerequisite. node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b expressly separates offer attribution from funding and fulfilment.",
    "The circular defines distributors in the context of SFC-authorised funds, supporting that contextual restriction. Its paragraph 3.11 summary uses broader investment-product language. These representations do not establish paragraph 3.11's complete reach outside the circular's context.",
    "Paragraph 9 says incentives may be gifts; incentive or guaranteed-return status alone does not establish prohibition. Aggregate gift classifications require assessment of individual components and sufficient evidence before concluding that none qualifies. A separate fee discount cannot exempt a distinct non-discount gift.",
    "The source does not require actual distraction, payment, receipt, acceptance or a public invitation for the gift restriction. Adding those requirements would permit offers without source support. Conversely, the gift result must not be presented as a section 103 offence or as overall legality.",
    "External Code of Conduct paragraphs 3.11 and 2.3, SFO section 103 and relevant exemption provisions, the FAQ answer identified in footnote 3, and the Advertising Guidelines and supplements are not supplied. These are unnecessary to confirm the two express circular claims, but are needed for independent interpretation of the respective full standards. No external dependency IDs are available.",
    "No supplied source unit establishes a concrete effective interval. The candidates' temporal descriptions do not verify current or historical applicability; the FAQ's issue date does not establish those boundaries.",
    "The review assesses supplied representations and declared runtime semantics. No executing implementation or runtime evidence is supplied."
  ],
